{"chart":{"title":"Death rate from venomous snakes","subtitle":"Estimated annual number of deaths from snakebite envenoming per 100,000 people. Snakebite envenoming is a potentially fatal disease caused by toxins in the bite or spit of a venomous snake.","note":"To allow for comparisons between countries this metric is age-standardized.","citation":"GBD 2019 Snakebite Envenomation Collaborators (2022)","originalChartUrl":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/death-rate-from-snakebite-envenoming","selection":["World","India","Somalia","Indonesia","China","France","South Africa","Central African Republic","Brazil","United States"]},"columns":{"Age-standardized death rate from snakebite envenoming":{"titleShort":"Age-standardized death rate from snakebite envenoming","titleLong":"Age-standardized death rate from snakebite envenoming","descriptionShort":"Age-standardized death rate per 100,000 people from snakebite envenoming.","shortUnit":"","unit":"deaths per 100,000 people","timespan":"2019-2019","type":"Numeric","owidVariableId":816321,"shortName":"age_standardized_death_rate_per_100000","lastUpdated":"2023-11-21","citationShort":"GBD 2019 Snakebite Envenomation Collaborators (2022) – with minor processing by Our World in Data","citationLong":"GBD 2019 Snakebite Envenomation Collaborators (2022) – with minor processing by Our World in Data. “Age-standardized death rate from snakebite envenoming” [dataset]. GBD 2019 Snakebite Envenomation Collaborators, “Global mortality of snakebite envenoming between 1990 and 2019” [original data].","fullMetadata":"https://api.ourworldindata.org/v1/indicators/816321.metadata.json"}},"dateDownloaded":"2026-11-19"}